  ANALYTIC_AUTODIFF_MATCH = PASS
    closed form  max|err| 7.88e-07 (tol 1e-5) ; repo sampled max|err| 1.66e-03 over non-clip cells (tol 5e-3)

  FIXED POINT  d KL/d log sigma_n = 0  <=>  sigma_n^2 = sigma_o^2 + dmu^2
               sigma_n* = sqrt(sigma_o^2 + dmu^2) >= sigma_o, equality iff dmu=0
  SIGN         descent moves log sigma by -grad. When
               sigma_n^2 < sigma_o^2 + dmu^2 the gradient is NEGATIVE, the step
               is POSITIVE, and sigma INCREASES. Forward KL is minimised by widening.
  CONTRAST     reverse KL(new||old): d/dlog sigma_n = -1 + sigma_n^2/sigma_o^2,
               fixed point sigma_n* = sigma_o exactly. No widening incentive.
               check sg_o=sg_n=0.4 dmu=0.3: +9.54e-08 (expect 0)
  CEILING      the action clip at 0.9999 caps |y| at atanh = 4.9517, so once
               sigma_n >> 4.95 the sampled second moment stops tracking sigma_n^2
               and the same term becomes CONTRACTING. Quantified in part 2.

